description:
You are a Site Reliability Engineer (SRE) responding to a Severity 2 incident. You need to audit the DNS and SSL status of three critical external domains: google.com, amazon.com, and microsoft.com. 

1. DNS Audit: Use 'Google Admin Toolbox Dig' (https://toolbox.googleapps.com/apps/dig/) to perform an A record lookup for each domain. Record the first IP address returned.

2. SSL Audit: Use 'SSL Shopper' (https://www.sslshopper.com/ssl-checker.html) OR 'DigiCert SSL Checker' (https://www.digicert.com/help/) to check the SSL certificate for each domain. Record the Issuer (Organization) and the Expiration Date.

3. Evidence: Create a Firefox bookmark folder named 'Incident 2411 Audit'. Bookmark the specific result page (or tool page) for EACH of the 6 checks (3 DNS + 3 SSL).

4. Report: Create a JSON file at ~/Documents/audit_log.json with the following structure:
{
  "google.com": {
    "ip_address": "...",
    "ssl_issuer": "...",
    "ssl_expiry": "YYYY-MM-DD"
  },
  "amazon.com": { ... },
  "microsoft.com": { ... }
}

Ensure dates are in YYYY-MM-DD format.
